  "problem": "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $\\,T\\,$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\,T,$ find $\\,T(v).$\n\n| $T(v)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v\\,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -19\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
